quired even if the foreign course work has been accepted by a college or university in the United States. Program Manager Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310021-EXTENSN HOME EC PGM UNIT The Center of Innovation (COI) Quality Service Review (QSR) is looking for a Program Manager to oversee contracts and financial processes for the QSR program. The QSR program provides training, qualitative program evaluation, and workforce development to build behavioral health and child welfare service systems. Student Life Communications Specialist Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Looking for creative and passionate professional to join our team. The Student Life Communications Specialist provides strategic leadership for Student Life’s digital communications, marketing, branding, and student engagement technologies. This position manages and optimizes Crimson Connection, Student Life websites, social media, publications, and multimedia content to promote programs, services, events, and campus traditions. Working collaboratively with student leaders and campus partners, the specialist develops innovative communication strategies, provides platform training and support, and uses engagement analytics to increase student involvement and advance student success. CES County Program Assistant 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 310850-ADMIN AND PGM SUPP UNIT UNION CNTY New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service is seeking a motivated and community-focused County Program Assistant to support educational programs and outreach efforts in Union County. This position will assist with planning, coordinating, and delivering Extension programs that address local community needs, provide educational resources, and promote positive outcomes for youth, families, agriculture, and community members Apply Now First Name (required) 7a43884c Last Name (required) 659e442b Email (required) 1f2312ca Refer