nagement (IAM) platform by managing systems integrations, monitoring security and compliance, and maintaining accurate identity data. Collaborate with functional users, IT Governance, and technical teams to implement IAM solutions, perform audits, support system upgrades, and ensure secure, reliable access management across the university. Maintain system documentation and stay current with emerging IAM technologies and best practices.\n\nMust be authorized to work in the United States. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position.\n\nIndividuals who have completed college or university course work at an institution in a country other than the United States must obtain a complete evaluation of foreign transcripts, degrees, and the translation of other relevant employment documents prior to being offered employment at New Mexico State University. A foreign transcript evaluation is required any time foreign course work is used to meet an employment related credential requirement. An evaluation is required even if the foreign course work has been accepted by a college or university in the United States. Program Manager Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310021-EXTENSN HOME EC PGM UNIT The Center of Innovation (COI) Quality Service Review (QSR) is looking for a Program Manager to oversee contracts and financial processes for the QSR program. The QSR program provides training, qualitative program evaluation, and workforce development to build behavioral health and child welfare service systems. Student Life Communications Specialist Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 520830-STUDENT LIFE Looking for creative and passionate professional to join our team. The Student Life Communications Specialist provides strategic leadership for Student Life’s digital communications, marketing, branding, and student engagement technologies. This position manages and optimizes Crimson Connection, Student Life websites, social media, publications, and multimedia content to promote programs, services, events, and campus traditions. Working collaboratively with student leaders and campus partners, the specialist develops innovative communication strategies, provides platform training and support, and uses engagement analytics to increase student involvement and advance student success. CES County Program Assistant 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 310850-ADMIN AND PGM SUPP UNIT UNION CNTY New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service is seeking a motivated and community-focused County Program Assistant to support educational programs and outreach efforts in Union County. This position will assist with planning, coordinating, and delivering Extension programs that address local community needs, provide educational resources, and promote positive outcomes for youth, families, agriculture, and community members Apply Now First Name (required) 10695ea5 Last Name (required) 7964440a Email (required) 74ffd7fb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
