    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/program-coordinator-nmsu-satellite-location-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Program Coordinator - NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Program Coordinator 504075 NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 17 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Michael Patrick, 575-202-4253, jmpat@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension is seeking a Program Coordinator II to support the development and implementation of agricultural and economic programming in Las Vegas, New Mexico. This position will coordinate program activities, assist with farm education and training, and support day-to-day farm operations and participant activities. Position Details Position Title: Program Coordinator College/Division: Cooperative Extension Service Department: 311100-EXTENSN ECONOMICS Location: NMSU satellite location Offsite Location (if applicable): Las Vegas NM Target Hourly/Salary Rate: 16.83 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Shift: Other Shift If Not a Standard Work Schedule: May work on weekends and evenings Job Duties and Responsibilities: Candidate must live in San Miguel County. Oversee the development, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of program activities to ensure program goals and objectives are met. Assist the Farm Manager with conducting education and training sessions; monitoring participants’ proper and safe use of farm equipment, tools, and facilities; maintaining farm buildings and structures; and obtaining necessary materials and supplies for planting, cultivating, and harvesting farm products. Serve as a liaison with community partners to provide program information and promote program activities, recruit farm participants, and develop and strengthen markets for farm-produced products. Conduct assessments of program activities, including education and training, production, markets and marketing, and farm management practices. Identify areas for improvement and implement appropriate actions to enhance program performance. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records related to program participants, employees, purchases, sales, production activities, and other program operations. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 1 years of relevant experience, or higher degree. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, bu